From: ADP-XC7K160 board notes
Subject: [PATCH] net: adp-ethmac: phylib and the bit-banged MDIO bus

The driver reads the link state of the PHY through phylib. The MDIO bus of
the SoC is the bit-banged MDIO of LiteEth: two CSRs for MDC, the direction and
the data.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/litex/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/litex/Kconfig
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 config ADP_ETHMAC
 	tristate "ADP-XC7K160 Ethernet MAC with DMA"
 	depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM && HAS_DMA
+	select PHYLIB
+	select MDIO_BITBANG
 	help
 	  The Ethernet MAC with DMA of the LiteX SoC of the Andes ADP-XC7K160
 	  board: the MAC core of LiteEth with a DMA front end on the coherent
